WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.686
The immigration to MAID pipeline.

00:00:02.636 --> 00:00:04.545
From arrival to death.

00:00:04.545 --> 00:00:09.363
This page documents a six-stage pipeline using only official government data.

00:00:09.363 --> 00:00:14.318
Stage one: Canada selects immigrants based on credentials through Express Entry.

00:00:14.318 --> 00:00:20.818
Stage two: those credentials are not recognised upon arrival, trapping skilled workers in survival employment.

00:00:20.818 --> 00:00:26.977
Stage three: immigrants wait years for a family doctor — six point five million Canadians have none.

00:00:26.977 --> 00:00:35.136
Stage four: without healthcare access and trapped in poverty, immigrants develop chronic conditions, disabilities, and mental health crises.

00:00:35.136 --> 00:00:41.818
Stage five: when they seek help, some are offered MAID instead of treatment — the same pattern documented with veterans.

00:00:41.818 --> 00:00:53.954
Stage six: each MAID death saves the healthcare system eight thousand one hundred and fifty dollars while reducing demand for the long-term care facilities that Brookfield Asset Management — the PM's former employer — owns globally.

00:00:53.954 --> 00:01:01.079
Every stage is documented from IRCC, Statistics Canada, Health Canada, CIHI, and corporate filings.

00:01:01.079 --> 00:01:03.693
The pipeline is not hypothetical.

00:01:03.693 --> 00:01:05.568
It is operational.

00:01:05.568 --> 00:01:07.943
Six documented stages.

00:01:07.943 --> 00:01:10.829
Each stage uses official government data.

00:01:10.829 --> 00:01:13.193
Each stage feeds the next.

00:01:13.193 --> 00:01:15.159
The data connections.

00:01:15.159 --> 00:01:18.443
Each stage transition has official government data.

00:01:18.443 --> 00:01:22.329
IRCC data shows who is selected and their credentials.

00:01:22.329 --> 00:01:28.874
StatsCan's longitudinal immigration database tracks employment outcomes showing credential underutilization.

00:01:28.874 --> 00:01:32.738
CIHI data shows healthcare utilization gaps for immigrants.

00:01:32.738 --> 00:01:37.306
CMHC data shows housing cost burden by immigration status.

00:01:37.306 --> 00:01:41.988
Health Canada MAID reports show eligibility categories and demographics.

00:01:41.988 --> 00:01:48.113
Brookfield's SEC filings show portfolio composition including healthcare and seniors housing.

00:01:48.113 --> 00:01:51.818
The PM's ethics filings show his Brookfield holdings.

00:01:51.818 --> 00:01:54.863
No single data source proves the pipeline.

00:01:54.863 --> 00:02:04.511
Together, they document a system where each stage creates the conditions for the next — and the financial beneficiary at the end is connected to the political leadership that maintains the system.

00:02:04.511 --> 00:02:06.511
The complete pipeline.

00:02:06.511 --> 00:02:08.693
Import skilled workers.

00:02:08.693 --> 00:02:10.704
Deny their credentials.

00:02:10.704 --> 00:02:12.704
Deny them healthcare.

00:02:12.704 --> 00:02:14.715
Push them into poverty.

00:02:14.715 --> 00:02:16.943
When they break, offer death.

00:02:16.943 --> 00:02:20.477
Profit from reduced demand for the care they never received.

00:02:20.477 --> 00:02:25.443
The PM who maintains this system holds stock options in the company that benefits from it.

00:02:25.443 --> 00:02:28.056
This is not a conspiracy theory.

00:02:28.056 --> 00:02:40.647
It is documented institutional architecture where each policy decision — credential barriers, physician shortages, housing financialization, MAID expansion, Brookfield's portfolio — is individually rational and collectively lethal.

00:02:40.647 --> 00:02:48.920
The immigration to MAID pipeline is the most complete expression of the institutional capture documented across two hundred and fourteen pages on this site.

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:54.977
It begins with a lie — come to Canada, we want your skills — and ends with a death that saves the system money.

00:02:54.977 --> 00:02:57.659
Every stage is a policy choice.

00:02:57.659 --> 00:03:01.227
Every policy choice serves institutional interests.

00:03:01.227 --> 00:03:03.738
Every institution is captured.
